Which statement matches the diagram?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (-2,0) node[left] {$A$}--(2,0) node[right] {$B$}; \draw (0,-2) node[below] {$C$}--(0,2) node[above] {$D$}; \draw (0.32,0)--(0.32,0.32)--(0,0.32);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Are lines $p$ and $q$ perpendicular?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0) node[right] {$p$}; \draw (255:2.1)--(75:2.1) node[above] {$q$}; \node at (35:0.95) {$75^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which pair of sides is perpendicular in rectangle $JKLM$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (0,0) node[below left] {$J$}--(3,0) node[below right] {$K$}--(3,1.8) node[above right] {$L$}--(0,1.8) node[above left] {$M$}--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What does the small square at $O$ tell you?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (-2,-1) node[left] {$E$}--(2,1) node[right] {$F$}; \draw (-1,2) node[above] {$G$}--(1,-2) node[below] {$H$}; \node[below left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0); \coordinate (A) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(2,1)$); \coordinate (B) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(-1,2)$); \draw (A)--($(A)+(B)-(O)$)--(B);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
